  [patch-notes list](https://playvalorant.com/en-us/news/tags/patch-notes/) and
  the notes for 10.00, 10.04, 11.08, 12.00, 12.05, 13.00, 13.01, 13.04 and 13.06.
  Riot's agent pages render most ability names as unlabeled icons, so they
  confirm roles but not every ability name.
- [valorant-api.com](https://valorant-api.com/v1/version), a community mirror of
  the game's own files, read at build **release-13.06** (built 2026-09-25):
  [agents](https://valorant-api.com/v1/agents?isPlayableCharacter=true) (29,
  with role and every ability name) and
  [weapons](https://valorant-api.com/v1/weapons) (21, with class and fire mode).
  Not Riot's site, but it is the game data itself; used for names, classes and
  fire modes, never for pictures.
- Press, only where Riot's pages are silent: [Liquipedia, Patch 9.04](https://liquipedia.net/valorant/Patch_9.04)
  (Vyse) and [Sheep Esports](https://www.sheepesports.com/articles/valorant-everything-about-veto-the-new-senegalese-agent/en)
  (Veto). Liquipedia's other pages and valorant.fandom returned 403.
- Dropped: TheSpike's weapons list, which the previous draft cited. It still
