## What is in VALORANT today

- **Patch 13.06**, 2026-09-22, in **Season 2026 Act 5** (Riot: "Stage V26A5",
  which began with [13.04](https://playvalorant.com/en-us/news/game-updates/valorant-patch-notes-13-04/)
  on 2026-08-18). [13.06](https://playvalorant.com/en-us/news/game-updates/valorant-patch-notes-13-06/)
  added the **Warden** rifle, Agent Mastery and a menu revamp. No 13.07 notes
  were published by 2026-10-10.
- **29 agents**, the same 29 on Riot's agents page and in the 13.06 game data:
  8 Duelists, 7 Initiators, 7 Controllers, 7 Sentinels. Since mid-2024:
  Vyse (Episode 9 Act 2, patch 9.04; the previous draft said Act 1, fixed),
  Tejo (patch 10.00, Season 2025), Waylay (patch 10.04, Riot: "our newest
  Duelist"), Veto (Sentinel, Season 2025 Act 6 / patch 11.08, `uncertain`:
  Riot's 11.08 notes do not name him), Miks (Controller, patch 12.05, Riot:
  "Act 2 starts now with the arrival of Miks"). The launch and episode acts of
  the older agents are the long-standing ones, not re-read today.
- **21 guns**, the same 21 in the 13.06 game data. Riot's Arsenal lists 20: the
  **Warden** is not on it yet, but Riot's 13.06 notes describe it ("Weapon
  Class: Rifle", "the latest automatic Rifle", 2x scope), so it is not marked
  uncertain. The **Bandit** sidearm arrived in
  [patch 12.00](https://playvalorant.com/en-us/news/game-updates/valorant-patch-notes-12-00/)
  (2026-01-06, start of Season 2026).
- **Class names.** Riot's Arsenal says Sidearms, SMGs, Shotguns, Rifles,
  Snipers, Heavies, Melee; the game data says Sidearms, SMGs, Shotguns,
  Assault Rifles (Warden: Rifles), Sniper Rifles, Heavy Weapons. The groups use
  the game data's words where both Riot sources agree in substance: the old
  "Machine Guns" group (in neither) is now **Heavy Weapons**, id
  `heavy_weapons` (nothing has shipped, so the ids moved). "Rifles" is kept
  because the Arsenal and the Warden both use it.
- **5 agent weapons**, the abilities that put a weapon in the agent's hands and
  swap the HUD's ammo for theirs: Jett's Blade Storm, Chamber's Headhunter and
  Tour De Force, Raze's Showstopper, Neon's Overdrive (spellings from the game
  data). The four agents since 2025 add none: Tejo (Armageddon), Waylay
  (Convergent Paths), Veto (Evolution) and Miks (Bassquake) have no weapon
  ultimate. Miks's Harmonize is an equipped ability, but it targets an ally
  (Riot: "Fire on an ally ... Combat Stim"), not a gun, so it is not listed.
  "Agent weapons" is our group name, not Riot's.

**Fire modes** (`fireMode`) are each gun's primary fire. The game data marks
Classic, Shorty, Ghost, Sheriff, Bandit, Bucky, Guardian, Marshal, Outlaw and
Operator semi-automatic and leaves the rest as automatic; the catalog writes
the bolt-action Marshal and Operator as `bolt` and the Bucky as `pump`.
Headhunter (`semi`) and Tour De Force (`bolt`) are from guides only, so both
carry `uncertain`. No stats or prices are in the format.

## HUD states

From public guides (e.g. [ONE Esports, understanding the HUD](https://www.oneesports.gg/valorant/valorant-beginners-guide-understanding-the-hud/)),
**not checked on a real frame**. HUD scale, colours and crosshair are the
player's own settings, so every position below is approximate.

| state | what is on screen | what the Core could read |
|---|---|---|
| **Buy phase** | Round start; the buy menu (full-screen grid of guns by class, with prices) opens on a key; a countdown at the top; barriers hold players in spawn | The buy menu covers the HUD: read nothing for aim. The gun the player ends up holding is read once the menu closes. Could mark "round starting" |
| **In round** | Bottom-centre: health, armour, the agent's ability row (C, Q, E with charge pips, ultimate X with its point ring). Bottom-right: credits, and above them the weapon inventory (gun silhouettes, the held one highlighted; spike icon on top for the carrier). Ammo near the ability row. Top: round timer, score, both teams' portraits. Minimap top-left | The **agent** from the ability row (always shown, unique per agent: D122 picture teaching). The **gun** from its silhouette in the inventory column, or its ammo count; there is **no gun name as text**. An agent weapon replaces the ammo display while it is out |
| **Scoped** | Right-click with a scoped gun: Operator, Marshal, Outlaw, Warden (2x) and rifle/SMG ADS zoom; snipers show a full-screen scope overlay | A full scope overlay hides the HUD centre; the gun is the one read just before. Scoped is itself a cue (useful for a sniper's Smart Action) |
| **Flashed** | Flashes (e.g. Phoenix, Breach, Skye, KAY/O, Reyna, Yoru) white the screen out for a moment | Nothing is readable; hold the last answer, do not re-detect |
| **Dead / spectating** | The view follows a teammate; that player's name and agent show at the bottom; the HUD shows **their** abilities and gun | Must not be read as the player's own agent or gun. Needs its own cue (the spectating label) before anything acts |
| **Round banners** | Full-width banners: round won / lost, spike planted, last player standing, match point | Cover the centre for a second or two; a cue that the round state changed, nothing to read for aim |
| **Menus** | Pause/settings, the agent select screen (before the match: every agent's portrait, the locked-in one highlighted), scoreboard (Tab), map | Agent select is the one place the agent is **named as text** (and shown large): a possible one-time read at match start. Otherwise read nothing |

## Class: Rainbow-style

VALORANT is **Rainbow-style** (picker driven), confirmed:

- The **agent** is what the owner picks, as he picks a Siege operator. Its
  ability row is always on screen in play and unique to the agent, so it can be
  taught as a picture (D122); agent select names it as text once per match.
- The **gun** is never printed as a name in play (guides above): only its
  silhouette in the inventory column and its ammo. So it is **not name-reading**;
  a gun is taught as a picture, or picked from All guns.
- It is **not "pass"**: both agents and guns are fixed, published lists.

Unlike Siege, the agent does not limit the guns (any agent buys any gun), which
is why the guns are a Fortnite-style pool with All guns.

## Update the list

- **A new agent:** add it at the end of its role's group with
  `loadout.pool` = every gun id (and its own ability weapon, if any), and add
  its id to every gun's `usedBy`. Check its ultimate in the game data
  (valorant-api.com agents) for a new agent weapon.
- **A new gun:** add it at the end of its class, put its id in every agent's
  pool, and give it `usedBy` = every agent.
- Then `asOf`, `season`, and `node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js`.
